Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which the ACMA may have regard.
A determination under this section may deal with ancillary or incidental matters, including the protection of the privacy of information transmitted in connection with a call to an emergency service number.
A determination under this section may deal with performance standards, including (but not limited to) performance standards relating to:
(a) the answering of calls to emergency service numbers; and
(b) delays in transferring calls made to an emergency service number to the appropriate emergency service organisation; and
(c) the handling of complaints about emergency call services.
Subsections (4) and (5) do not, by implication, limit subsection (1).
A determination under this section is a legislative instrument.
In making a determination under this section, the ACMA may apply, adopt or incorporate (with or without modification) any matter contained in a code or standard proposed or approved by a body or association, either:
(a) as in force or existing at a particular time; or
